WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
<b>Baseball Team</b>

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.030
Seriously, what the hell?

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:07.870
I was chilling out at home after the game.
Why are we all back here again?

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.760
Seems our second round opponents
tomorrow, Seiwa Middle, are crazy good.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:16.370
They beat Koutou Middle 10-2
in a game called after the fifth.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:17.690
Wow.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:21.890
I thought Koutou and Seiwa
were supposed to be evenly matched.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.680
I heard they found a coach who
knows his stuff a few years back.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.170
They scored ten runs, but their playstyle
revolves entirely around small ball.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:33.010
Small ball?

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:07.060
Seiwa Middle are
stronger than I anticipated.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:08.810
<b>Mutsuko's Special Training</b>

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.830
I called you all here so we can come up
with ways to deal with their offense.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.020
In particular, their base stealing.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.730
Base stealing?

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:21.160
The main focus of their batters
will be getting runners on base.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:25.130
And once on base, they'll attempt
to steal at every opportunity.

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:26.440
Bunts will be a factor, too.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:29.500
As soon as they see any kind of opening,
they'll try to advance the runners.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.960
Aside from their cleanup,
they're all fast runners.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.370
You sure the other team's catcher
wasn't just bad?

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.180
That's totally a thing. If the catcher sucks,
you can steal bases for fun.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:44.630
I don't think Anita will
give them such an easy ride.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.090
Darn tootin'!

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:50.190
I tol' him straight up my arm'd stop 'em
runnin' as freely as they did in that game.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.150
But Cap's still insistin'
we practice stoppin' 'em.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:57.290
The catcher's arm isn't the only thing
that prevents base stealing.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:00.530
The pitcher needs to do
slide steps and pickoffs.

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:02.240
The catcher can't do it alone.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:07.430
Pickoffs aren't something
I'm comfortable with yet.

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.040
I have my hands full just
pitching at the batter.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.150
Okay, then.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.250
If that's how it is, it's best we practice.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.780
After all, pickoffs are an
important part of my basework.

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:17.760
Oh, yeah.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:21.010
Well, we're all already here, so might as well.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:21.720
Yeah.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.420
We don't have a lot of time,
so I don't know how far we'll get,

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:27.180
but let's give it a go.

00:03:27.850 --> 00:03:30.170
<i>Give it a go, huh?</i>

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.730
All right. Let's start
with first base pickoffs.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:39.970
Chisato, pretend you're on the
opposing team and try stealing a base.

00:03:39.970 --> 00:03:41.200
Roger.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:46.420
Mutsuko and Anita, do everything
you can to stop Chisato from stealing.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.040
We're starting with runners?

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:50.250
Yeah, we won't have time otherwise.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.510
All right. Play!

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:56.720
Balk!

00:03:56.720 --> 00:03:57.250
Huh?

00:03:57.540 --> 00:04:02.220
No good. You can't stop halfway on
a pickoff attempt if your foot's on the rubber.

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.180
My foot's <i>not</i> on it. I moved it off.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:06.780
If you don't release,

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.270
you have to step way back from
the rubber or a balk gets called.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.710
You didn't do that just then, so you
should've committed to throwing it to first.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:16.980
All right, let's go again.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:19.200
R-Right...

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.590
<i>This is hard.</i>

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:27.060
<i>It's super hard concentrating on the runner
and slide stepping and all that junk...</i>

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:30.410
Balk!

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:31.750
Again?!

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.960
Not "again." A balk's a balk whenever it's called.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.540
When you step out with your left foot,

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.120
you have to point it at
first base, but you didn't.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:45.510
You rushed your throw
and only twisted from the waist.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.470
And what's more, your swivel was too slow.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.180
Chisato strolled back to first.

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:55.140
If you throw like that, you'll embolden
the runners, and they'll take bigger leads.

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:57.020
You need to speed it up.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.560
All right. Again.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.110
<i>What a nag.</i>

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:03.070
<i>I'm trying my best here...</i>

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:05.650
Balk!

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:06.490
Huh?

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:09.240
Heya.

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.870
Your glove didn't come to a stop.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.330
In the set position, a balk's called if your
glove doesn't come to a complete stop.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.540
All right. Again!

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.940
<i>And there we have it.</i>

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:26.160
<i>When Daigo says, "let's give it a go,"
it's never a casual training session.</i>

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:33.520
<b>Six Months Ago</b>

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.710
Since the baseball team is just us six now,

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:36.520
I'd like to preliminarily decide positions
so we can run defense drills and so on.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:42.240
First, Tanba-san. You were a starter on
third last year, so I'd like you to stay there.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.610
S-Sure.

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:45.200
I'll take second.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.960
Shortstop for me, then.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:48.950
Ooh! Outfield for me please!

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.880
Anywhere's fine as long as I get game-time.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.030
First base is free.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.140
Th-Then, first it is!

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:00.880
Pitcher?

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:05.030
Yeah. We don't have a pitcher right now, you see.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:10.890
Well, yeah, but I'm sure one of
the new sign-ups in spring will want to pitch.

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.310
Spring's way too late.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.880
We won't know if we can
throw them straight into a game,

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:20.690
so we need to train up at least 
one pitcher from our current roster.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:27.530
Based on skill, I think either Tao
or Sawa-san will be our best bet.

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:31.740
They're both talented, so I think 
they'd pick it up quite quickly.

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:35.450
Excuse me? No way am I gonna pitch!

00:06:35.800 --> 00:06:36.660
Huh?

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.440
Since Little League,
I've only ever played shortstop!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.490
I have zero interest in
playing any other position.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:45.070
Right... Sawa-san, what about—

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:46.340
Nope and nope!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:50.590
You can't split up the Yayoi-Tao
middle-infielder dream team.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.030
Sorry, Shigeno.

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:54.910
I also have zero interest in pitching.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:58.820
Shigeno-kun!

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.090
Did Tao and Yayoi agree to pitch?

00:07:02.090 --> 00:07:04.330
Nope. Both said no.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:05.770
So what are we going to do?

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.610
Well, I can't force anyone into doing it.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.190
Oh well. Guess it's back
to the drawing board.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:13.780
Second!

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.300
Okay!

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:20.250
First!

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.710
Bring it on!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.010
Whoa! Kandori, that's some arm you've got!

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:32.640
You think so?

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.720
First isn't the place for an arm like that.

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:37.680
Oh, how about third, then?

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:42.640
Third, huh? That sounds kinda cool...

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:46.860
Forget bases for now.
Can you throw a fastball at me?

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:50.040
M-Me? Pitch? Really?

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:53.620
Kan-chan as a pitcher, huh?
I never even considered her.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:56.870
With your arm, pitching might
suit you down to the ground.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.200
Uh, r-right.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:01.160
Here I go!

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.830
Okay!

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:10.130
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:13.070
Good. Keep 'em coming!

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.360
Uh, okay.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:32.440
Dead already?

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.880
Maybe I was being a bit unreasonable...

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:42.320
Too much, too much.

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:47.760
Good work today.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.840
Yeah, you too. Good work.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.960
Hey, Sakura.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:56.900
How do you feel about
pitching from tomorrow?

00:08:57.730 --> 00:09:02.890
You have amazing control...
when we play catch.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.490
Yikes, you're asking <i>me</i> now?

00:09:05.490 --> 00:09:07.230
What is this? Eenie, meenie, miney, moe?

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:14.530
I didn't realize it until now, but I think
you'd take to pitching quite easily.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.210
N-No way! Not happening!

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:23.330
My throws are slow, and all eyes are
on you when you're on the mound!

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:27.330
Just get Tao or Yayoi to do it!
Or maybe get Kan-chan to train up a bit...

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:31.340
Whatever you do,
there's absolutely no <i>way</i> I can do it!

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.260
Just give it a go.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:43.030
I'll help you out.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:48.270
If you want, you can throw as many pitches
as you like at me every single day.

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.290
Me... pitching...

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.760
Since it's your first time,
let's give it a go and see how we do.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.810
<i>Give it a go, huh?</i>

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:06.250
All right.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:13.840
<i>She has good form.</i>

00:10:21.440 --> 00:10:23.510
Okay, nice ball!

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:26.060
Uh, right!

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.020
What's going on here?
First Kandori, then Mutsuko.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:33.380
Shigeno's kind of all over the place.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.380
This might not be a bad idea, though.

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:37.860
I like third better, I think.

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.010
Sakura.

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:50.460
Try to consciously transfer more of your
weight to your front leg as you throw.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:52.540
Okay, I'll try!

00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.890
<i>Wait, wasn't this meant to be casual?</i>

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.350
I need... a breather.

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.570
We can call it a day there.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:13.220
Your core's pretty weak.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:16.780
Daily runs every morning and
after practice should fix that.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.990
What?!

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:48.240
This is your first time 
pitching to a batter,

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:50.230
but just aim for my mitt like always.

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:51.460
Right!

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.820
Whoa! That was real nice!

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:06.620
High to the inside this time!
You've got good control, Mutsuko!

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:10.690
Don't just admire them.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.510
This is batting practice too, you know.
You're meant to try and hit them.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.420
Oh, I have permission to hit them?

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.510
Okay, nice pitching.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.340
What was "nice" about <i>that</i>?!
They hit every single one!

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:47.620
It's pretty obvious I'm not
cut out to be a pitcher.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.080
Yeah, but you were only throwing fastballs.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.970
That's why we're going to add
more weapons to your arsenal.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:53.460
What?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.670
Can you come over to my house tomorrow?
It's Saturday and all.

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.590
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:00.590
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:13:04.460 --> 00:13:06.490
What's with that outfit?

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:10.470
Huh? Well, uh, I mean,
you told me not to wear a skirt.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.770
Well, whatever. Get on over here.

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:17.730
Wait, didn't you have a pool here before?

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:22.000
Yeah, but we got rid of it
so we'd have more room to practice.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.490
Wow.

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.070
<i>I swear, rich people...</i>

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.030
Good to see you!

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:29.330
H-Hello!

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:31.850
We haven't properly met yet, have we?

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:35.730
I'm Izumi, Daigo's big sis and
former Fuurin Middle baseball player.

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:38.380
Thank you for looking out for my brother.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.380
O-Oh, no problem.

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:41.540
My name is Sakura Mutsuko.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:45.480
I've heard so much about you
from Tanba-san and the others.

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:46.590
I'm a big fan!

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:49.530
Stop, you're embarrassing me.

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.180
I guess, unlike my bro,
<i>I</i> didn't drag the team down.

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:58.370
I wanted you to learn
how to throw breaking balls.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:14:00.520
I figured seeing them up 
close was the easiest way.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:02.420
Breaking balls?

00:14:04.090 --> 00:14:05.820
Pay attention to how the ball moves.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:06.670
Okay.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:09.660
Here it comes.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:17.460
A-Amazing! It curved!

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.480
That was a slider.

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:21.790
This is the weapon that will 
make your fastballs shine.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.630
Yeah, I wanna learn how
to do that. Please teach me!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:27.410
Put your middle finger on the stitching.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:28.590
Yeah, like that.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:32.160
Don't twist. Slice it like... this.

00:14:32.160 --> 00:14:34.090
Don't twist, slice.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.270
Okay! Now you give it a try.

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:43.860
Great! That curved.

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:45.970
Really? Awesome!

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.360
Hey, good pitch.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.820
For a first go, that was
excellent, Mutsuko-chan.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:51.940
Thank you so much!

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.290
Nice, Mutsuko-chan!

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.450
Good, Mutsuko-chan!

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.090
That's it, Mutsuko!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:10.300
Good, Mutsuko!

00:15:15.050 --> 00:15:17.740
I-I'm sorry, Shigeno-kun! Are you okay?!

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.680
That was awesome, Mutsuko!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.270
That slider just now was <i>perfect</i>!

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.360
You've come on leaps and bounds.
Let's keep this up!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:28.320
I'll catch all your pitches.

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:30.780
Okay!

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:34.380
Okay, time to take a break
and have some tea.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:38.920
Good luck with that. Those two can't
hear you. They're totally in the zone.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:40.120
Oh, my.

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.390
You're only using your hand
and trying to force it to curve.

00:15:43.390 --> 00:15:45.090
Try using your arm more.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:48.050
Aw, don't they look so cute together?

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.010
Yeah. You picked up on those vibes too?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.320
And you know something?

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:56.150
I get the feeling, if anything,
Mutsuko-chan's the one who's interested.

00:15:56.150 --> 00:15:58.520
Oh, really? And what about Daigo?

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:01.600
He's useless. He's totally oblivious.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.980
Oh, boy.

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:05.500
Like father, like son.

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:16.720
Nice ball!

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:19.570
I didn't think you'd pick it up this quickly.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:22.160
You're a natural at pitching, Mutsuko-chan!

00:16:22.360 --> 00:16:23.620
You think so?!

00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:27.090
Yep. You might become their trusty ace yet.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:28.570
Yay!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.850
Well, it's not game-ready just yet.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:35.200
That depends entirely on you.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:35.760
Ow.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:43.490
All right. Should we get back to it?

00:16:43.490 --> 00:16:45.270
This is another kind of grip.

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.140
That one looks difficult.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:51.610
With how you pitch, I think
you'll actually find it pretty easy.

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:54.320
Sis, what are you showing her?

00:16:54.730 --> 00:16:59.610
The sinker. I mean, I think it's time 
she learned another breaking ball.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:03.800
Hold on. It's too soon.
She only just learned the slider.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.290
Why? It's better to have more 
weapons at your disposal.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:12.880
That's true, but breaking balls already
put a strain on the shoulder and elbow.

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:16.730
That's why I'm showing her the pitches
that put the least strain on those areas.

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:21.800
Instead of learning them all at once,
it's better to get them down pat, one by one.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.270
You don't have time for that.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.480
You want to use them in the spring, right?

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:26.480
Um, Shigeno-kun?

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.190
I've made my own calculations!

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.650
Okay, then let's hear them!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:33.870
It's none of your business!

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:34.610
Shigeno-kun, I...

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:38.890
Ah, but you're not a pitcher!
Mutsuko-chan's the one pitching!

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:41.920
There are things the catcher
can see more clearly!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:41.920
Please stop, Shigeno-kun.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:44.620
I'm telling you it's not
your place to decide!

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:47.780
I'm the captain of the Fuurin baseball team!

00:17:45.100 --> 00:17:47.070
Shigeno-kun.

00:17:47.780 --> 00:17:49.470
Shigeno!

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:50.370
Yeah?

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:50.370
What is it?

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.000
Um, uh...

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.630
See? She's all flustered because of you!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.090
Huh?! It's because you're going overboard!

00:17:57.090 --> 00:17:59.550
Teaching her stuff we didn't even ask for!

00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.550
<i>They're both called Shigeno...</i>

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.260
Who do you think you are?! You're just Daigo!

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.600
What the hell does that mean?

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:06.560
Anyway, you're butting in
where you don't belong!

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:06.560
Da... Da... Da...

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.770
Shut the hell up, Daigo!

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.230
No, you shut up!

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.660
Daigo!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:16.150
<i>Oh, wow. She called him by his first name?</i>

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:22.030
U-Um, I... want to be useful
sooner rather than later,

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:24.250
so I'd like to learn the sinker.

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:25.750
Okay, Daigo?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.420
<i>I used his first name for the first time.</i>

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:36.080
Oh, really? Well, if you're
all right with it, let's get to it!

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.010
<i>Yup, thought so.</i>

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:47.850
<i>It's classic Daigo, failing to notice how
much this girl's heart is pounding.</i>

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:52.670
Nice ball!

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:54.690
You're getting into your groove, Mutsuko!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.650
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.650
<b>Fuurin Academy Private Middle School</b>

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.530
All right!

00:19:06.710 --> 00:19:10.320
Mutsuko's pitching is evolving fast.

00:19:10.320 --> 00:19:14.960
If you add breaking balls to her precision,
nobody's getting a clean hit.

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.340
Is that "Coach" Shigeno's doing?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.680
Hey, Daigo.

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:21.920
How were my sliders today?

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:24.970
I tried holding on
to the ball a bit longer.

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:29.180
Yeah, I think that'll
increase their precision.

00:19:29.590 --> 00:19:31.390
You think so too?

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:40.950
Good work, Daigo.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:42.070
See you, Daigo.

00:19:42.070 --> 00:19:43.900
We're off, Daigo.

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:45.730
What's that about?

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.860
All the girls are calling Shigeno
 by his first name now.

00:19:49.860 --> 00:19:51.580
Do they think he's a mascot?

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:58.980
It made me happy that I was able
to get Tao and Yayoi out today.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:03.130
Once your accuracy with breaking balls
improves, you'll get even more outs.

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:07.420
But if someone amazing
joins the team in the spring,

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.120
I won't be pitching anymore.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.580
You're honestly worried about that?

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:18.180
In no time at all, your pitching
has improved by a crazy amount.

00:20:18.180 --> 00:20:23.360
I believe in your abilities, Mutsuko.
And anyway, I consider you Fuurin's ace now.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.690
<i>He keeps calling me Mutsuko...</i>

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:29.530
Okay!

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:33.970
See you tomorrow.

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:35.530
See you, Daigo.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:43.170
Mutsuko, when did you start 
calling me by my first name?

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:45.580
The other girls do it now, too...

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.260
Well, not that it matters.

00:20:48.320 --> 00:20:49.350
See ya!

00:20:50.790 --> 00:20:52.800
You only just realized <i>now</i>?!

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.900
Heya.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:02.490
All right. Again!

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.200
Again?!

00:21:04.480 --> 00:21:08.080
Senpai, she ain't gettin'
it perfect by tomorrow.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:11.140
All this'll do is make us
self-destruct 'cause we're focusin'

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:13.700
on the runner an' forgettin' 'bout the batter!

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:17.170
Yeah. As a pitcher, I agree with what she said.

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:22.880
It's impossible to learn quick pickoffs
 and slide steps in one day.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:26.910
Someone who's never pitched
before wouldn't understand.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:29.970
I never said this was going to be easy.

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:35.180
But as we're up against a running team,
I want to take the fight to them!

00:21:36.860 --> 00:21:40.820
If we can't shackle Seiwa's runners,
we will lose tomorrow.

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:42.780
We still have time.

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.360
You can never be fully prepared,

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:49.200
but if there's still stuff we can do,
I want to do it before we take them on!

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:56.570
It's all good. Let's get on with it already, Daigo.

00:21:56.570 --> 00:21:58.210
The sun's starting to go down.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
Mifune Seiwa Middle School

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:02.670
Mifune Seiwa Middle School

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:06.210
Okay, last one. We'll call it a day after.

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:08.010
What, stopping already?

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.940
I don't want to wear us both out.

00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:13.520
Let's go into tomorrow's game
firing on all cylinders.

00:22:15.040 --> 00:22:16.430
Gotcha.

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:20.590
<i>Shigeno has hardly grown at all
since our little league days.</i>

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:22.670
<i>But me?</i>

00:22:25.650 --> 00:22:28.110
<i>I'm not the same guy I was back then.</i>

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:04.580
Hey, Andy, who do we play
after we beat Fuurin?

00:24:04.580 --> 00:24:07.720
What's that, Urabe? You think we've already won?

00:24:07.720 --> 00:24:10.480
They won't even get near my pitches.

00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:16.180
Before that, our small ball might throw them
off their game and make them self-destruct.

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:19.350
See? You're confident we're gonna win, too.

00:24:19.650 --> 00:24:22.380
Next time: "Extreme Small Ball."

00:24:21.350 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>Extreme Small Ball</b>

00:24:22.380 --> 00:24:24.450
Run to the stage of your dreams!
